pring is a  different story but we'll get to that a  little bit later in the survey an  interesting point here is that people  also gave an answer as to what quarter  of the year would be coming out the  majority prediction overall is the  second quarter which is april may and  june of 2017 if you've been waiting and  wondering when the book might come out  think spring of 2017 this seems  realistic to me just based on the amount  of time between the last two releases  which is the strong indication of how  long it takes him to get a book done the  next bit of data is how many years after  publication of the winds of winter will  it take for a dream of spring to be  published the stat that jumps out to me  here is that 21.2 percent answered never  twenty percent would be one out of every  five people pulled what seemed super  high to me I guess I've always had it in  the back of my mind that it's possible  the final book wouldn't get finished but  I don't think I'd ever vote that way  keep in mind that even though this is  the highest individual answer it means  that nearly eighty percent of people  answered that it would actually come out  the positive answers are just spread out  over different lengths of time in  general most of the answers are from  four to seven years with an overall  average of five point five four this  seems like a good educated guess to me  and I expect this is the way things will  turn out so if you think winds will be  out early next year that means a dream  of spring will be dropping in the winter  of 20 22 it sounds so long from now when  you say it like that but let's remember  that building worlds and writing great  stories isn't something that happens  overnight to go along with this we get  the most common responses as to why some  people believe a dream of spring won't  be published they include george RR  martin is old he's losing interest  lacking motivation george RR martin will  die he's slowing down and that he has a  slow writing pace first of all George  just had a birthday and turned 68 that's  not that old the average life expectancy  for men in the u.s. is around 75 with a  number of factors that could make that  higher the answer that he's losing  interest is the dumbest answer in my  opinion because a lot of things can  happen to slow down a creative process  but losing interest in the story you've  been thinking about for more than 20  years just isn't one of them in my  opinion wanted to take a break have a  hiatus work on something else so on and  so forth those are all reasonable  reasonable things that could pop up but  it's not like he doesn't work on other  projects concurrently I think stress is  a very real part of this process but I  can't see him losing interest in doing  what pretty much every writer sets out  to do in their lifetime this series is  his magnum opus he is slowing down has  some validity to it since I can imagine  that ending a story like this is pretty  daunting overall once you're going you  know once you hit the end it's probably  hard to wrap things up but I'm in the  camp of thinking that taking a little  more time will pay dividends to the  reader so this doesn't really  bother me slow writing pays well that is  what it is every writer is different so  most of us have been waiting for a long  time for the release of wind so we'll  just have to wait until it's done george  RR martin will die is a frightening  answer that i don't really want to think  about honestly like I said he isn't that  old and as far as I can tell all of his  faculties are intact I can see if he was  like 95 or even 88 but this is just  isn't something that seems likely it  would be unfortunate if something would  happen to his health but it's not the  sort of thing we need to worry about  last two sections of the graphic or  about whether a dream of spring will be  the last book in the series seventy  percent of people answered yes and I  tend to agree obviously the series could  be enjoyable for fans no matter how many  books there end up being but I tend to  think that the author would like to  finish we know he has other song of ice  and fire related works he wants to  complete and he has mentioned wanting to  write other genres as well I don't think  money prestige fame or anything else  really factors into it anymore at this  point he had a story in mind and the  most reasonable thing for him to do is  to complete it of the thirty percent of  people who don't think it will be the  last book the most common responses are  too much to write and wrap up there's  still money to be made it will be split  into two books george RR martin is bad  at predictions this was originally  supposed to be a trilogy after all none  of these answers are outside the realm  of possibility but i still think he is  at the point of wanting to finish part  of me thinks that coming up with new  ideas isn't the problem but instead  staying out of the weeds and just  heading straight to the finish line is  we have some evidence of this with the  last two books and the subsequent winds  of winter preview chapters we've seen  but overall I don't think he will run  into the same problem again and again I  guess it is possible that he might have  to chop dreams into two books but I  wouldn't expect that to happen unless  he's already written a bunch of chapters  for it at this point for those who  thought it wouldn't be the last book  57.7 percent said that they thought it  would get finished and forty two point  three percent said no the most common  answers here seemed to be the basically  the same as the people who thought the  winds would never come out in the first  place since I don't think he will add  another book to the series I can't  really offer much on this the last  section of the infographic gives a nice  overview on when the people surveyed  started reading the series if you're  wondering why there is such a big spike  in 2000  and while it's because that's when Game  of Thrones first aired on HBO the last  thing at the bottom tells us there was  no observable correlation between the  length of time participants had been a  fan and the predictions they made for  the release of winds of winter and a  dream of spring this means based on the  data that older a song of ice and fire  fans are no more pessimistic nor  optimistic than newer faint so what do  you guys think let me know in the  comments if you've been waiting for the  book and what you think will happen do  you think when the winner will be out  before Game of Thrones Season seven how  about a dream of spring do you think  it's going to be the same amount of time  we're going to wait or do you think that  it might come out a little bit faster or  if you're a complete du mer do you think  it'll never come up please like the  video if you think it's likable I  appreciate all the feedback I've been  getting and want to welcome all the new  subscribers I had a couple of people ask  me about a patreon account through my  Twitter so I'm thinking about starting  one let me know what you guys think if  you think it's a good idea thing with  patreon is it's great but it's hard to  get it started you know patreon that has  supporters obviously does better than  one that doesn't so I'm kind of like  button hesitant to start one without  much interest in now that I have some  interest i'm thinking more about doing  it also we're getting close to the  giveaway goal if you're not a subscriber  please subscribe now for your chance to  win i'm giving one of you guys a free  copy of the night of the Seven Kingdoms  when I hit eighteen thousand subscribers  all you have to do is leave a comment  but likes are also appreciated what I'll  do is I'll use one of the youtube  comment pickers that are out there I'll  search through the videos I've made  since the giveaway started and pick one  comment from each of those videos from  there I'll take all those names and pick 